    "body": "Problem:\r\n'isident' decides how env var names are parsed, which is more\r\n\"confusing\" than \"useful\":\r\n- Changing 'isident' (for 'define' or \"\\i\") can break `$NAME` expansion.\r\n- Its default byte ranges let multibyte names work on Windows (`$aあ`)\r\n  but not Unix (`$é`).\r\n\r\nSolution:\r\nIgnore 'isident' when parsing env var names.\r\n\r\nfollowup to https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42200 , @bfredl LGTY?\r\n",
    "closed_at": "2026-10-05T17:29:49Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "yeah. as the dot over the i, could remove the MSWIN specfic default for the 'isident' option now, as it only concerns buffer content, and that is the same across platforms:)",
